emma: Heads-up: found a subtle issue in the Kotlin SDK sample where redirects + retry interceptor drop Authorization and trigger refresh loops on some backends.

rick: interesting, short repro?

emma: sample app uses Retrofit + OkHttp, followRedirects=true, and a RetryInterceptor that retries on 307/308 and on 401 by refreshing token then retrying. Problem: when server returns a 307 to a different host, OkHttp strips credential headers for cross-host redirects by default. Our retry sees 401 on the redirected request, triggers refresh, but the original request that caused redirect already lost Auth so server 401s repeatedly.

priya: oof. So sequence: client -> A (307 to B without auth) -> B rejects -> interceptor refreshes -> retries original request (still possibly redirected) -> same thing -> loop.

dan: can you paste the retry snippet?

emma: snippet: 
```kotlin
class RetryInterceptor : Interceptor {
  override fun intercept(chain: Interceptor.Chain): Response {
    val req = chain.request()
    var resp = chain.proceed(req)
    if (resp.code == 307 || resp.code == 308) {
      // naive retry once to follow certain infra redirects
      resp.close()
      resp = chain.proceed(req)
    }
    if (resp.code == 401) {
      tokenProvider.refreshSync()
      val newReq = req.newBuilder().header("Authorization", "Bearer ${tokenProvider.get()}").build()
      resp.close()
      return chain.proceed(newReq)
    }
    return resp
  }
}
```

rick: ah, two issues: 1) OkHttp handles redirects internally before passing final response to interceptor in some cases; manual retrying on 307 can cause double-redirection or lost headers. 2) Credentials on cross-host redirects are dropped intentionally.

priya: fix ideas?

dan: simplest for sample app: do not retry on 307/308 in interceptor. Let OkHttp redirect. If you need to mutate headers for redirected host, implement a network interceptor (which sees intermediate responses) and explicitly copy headers when safe. Or pre-resolve host and attach per-host creds.

emma: we updated sample app to: a) remove naive 307 retry, b) convert auth refresh to single-flight async refresh, c) add note in README: "Redirects may strip Authorization header when cross-host; prefer network-interceptor or explicit host-scoped tokens."

rick: also add short test: backend that returns 307 to different host, ensure that Authorization is not observed at redirected host unless explicitly added.

priya: add runbook entry for on-call: signs include spikes of 307 then immediate 401s at downstream host, tokens refreshed rapidly but no reduction in 401 rate. Stack traces not helpful since redirect happens at HTTP layer.

ci-bot: CI pipeline: opened PR 4827 with sample changes, tests, and README update.

emma: will validate against OkHttp 4.11 and SDK alpha. Note Android <10 behavior differences for SNI/redirects; included compatibility note.

dan: thanks — super useful. Let's also update SDK docs "Auth patterns" with a short section: redirects and credential scope.

emma: PR incoming in an hour. :thumbsup:
